FireRed-style UI & interaction
A. Visual layer
   Tile-based rendering (not free-form pixels)
   Fixed resolution (240 × 160, scaled up)
   Pixel-perfect fonts
   4–5 color palettes per UI element
   Window frames with 9-slice borders
B. Interaction model
   D-pad navigation (up/down/left/right)
   Focus-based selection (not mouse-first)
   A / B buttons (confirm / cancel)
   Modal screens (menus pause background)
   Text appears letter-by-letter
C. UI components
   Menu lists
   Dialogue boxes
   Option selectors
   Yes / No prompts
   Scrollable lists with cursor

Approach: 
<canvas> for rendering
JS controls everything
Closest to a real GBA-style engine


