C. Input system

Code:

#js
window.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
  if (e.key === "ArrowDown") ui.moveCursor(1);
  if (e.key === "z") ui.confirm(); // A
  if (e.key === "x") ui.cancel();  // B
});

D. Text system
Monospaced
Printed character-by-character
Pauses on punctuation
Waits for input at end

Code:

#js
class TextPrinter {
  constructor(text) {
    this.text = text;
    this.index = 0;
  }

  update() {
    if (this.index < this.text.length) {
      this.index++;
    }
  }

  draw(ctx) {
    ctx.fillText(this.text.slice(0, this.index), 16, 120);
  }
}

E. State machine
FireRed is state-driven, not event-driven.
Example states:
OVERWORLD
MENU
DIALOG
LOCKED
Each state:
Owns input
Owns rendering priority
This prevents UI conflicts.


Do it in this exact order:
Fixed-resolution canvas
Keyboard input mapping
Basic state machine
Window rendering (9-slice)
Cursor + menu list
Text printer
Modal dialogs
Stop before content.
